PICTURE/ICON DRAW AND EDIT PROGRAM   Version 1.0
------------------------------------------------

README FILE
-----------


Welcome to my picture/icon viewer/editor. All the appropriate files are 
included for the Siena.  I have also included some example .PIC files 
which I downloaded from various bulletin boards.  Most of these were 
uploaded by anonymous donors, so I offer them my thanks and acknowledgments
for their hard work.

The ZIP file should contain the following files:

\APP\SNADRAW0.APP              Main Application 
\APP\SNADRAW\SNADRAW0.HLP      Optional Help File

README.NEW        This file

SNADRAW0.DOC      Documentation in Word for Windows format
SNADRAW0.TXT      Documentation in ASCII Text format

REGISTER.TXT      Details of how to register
HISTORY.TXT       History of program
LICENCE.TXT       Legal Agreement

Some example Icons and Pictures

\PIC\BLANK.PIC       Blank Background for S3a Icon
\PIC\BLANK2.PIC      Another Blank Background for S3a Icon
\PIC\COMMS.PIC       Example S3a Icon
\PIC\PSION.PIC       Example S3a Icon
\PIC\GREY.PIC        Example Picture drawn using program
\PIC\PORSCHE.PIC     Example Black only Picture
\PIC\UNDERGND.PIC    Map of London Underground
\PIC\MARILYN.PIC     The famous pinup picture

Installation:

1.    Put the APP file (SNADRAW0.APP) into an \APP\ directory.

2.    If you wish to use the optional On-Line Help, put the SNADRAWS0.HLP
      file into an \APP\SNADRAW\ Sub-directory.

3.    If you do not have one already, make a \PIC\ directory on any drive 
      (Not on a Flash SSD if you intend to edit the pictures) and put the
      example .PIC files into it.

4.    Install SNADRAW0.APP as covered in the manual using <Psion-I>. 
      Update the system screen if required.

5.    Select any picture to View/Edit, or press <Psion-N> to generate a 
      new picture.

6.    Until you register the program, you will have to work through the 
      'nag' screens.

7.    When you first run the program it will generate a SNADRAW.CFG file in
      the \OPD\ directory on your default drive, to keep the defaults.

8.    Play around with all of the menu commands to see the program's 
      capabilities.  The on-line help is very comprehensive, so you should 
      only have to resort to the documentation very occasionally.  To 
      encourage registration, I have 'switched out' all the various 'Save' 
      functions in unregistered copies.

